{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "20", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "24", "S": "18"}}, "news": [{"title": "We'll fix 22A errors, give genuine owners relief within days: Telangana revenue minister", "para": "Revenue minister Ponguleti Srinivas Reddy has acknowledged the ongoing property registration challenges, attributing them to administrative mistakes. These errors have led to incorrect listings of private properties, exacerbated by inconsistencies in land records and numbering. In response, the government is taking swift action to rectify these issues and aims to resume property registrations soon. A dedicated committee will be established to prevent future discrepancies.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/well-fix-22a-errors-give-genuine-owners-relief-within-days-telangana-revenue-minister/133363896?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-59922/133363896.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Maintenance paid, but Noida RWAs want tenants to shell out extra fees for using gym, pool", "para": "Tenants in Noida are now being charged extra for using amenities such as pools, as suggested by Resident Welfare Associations citing the need for security and maintenance funds. However, tenants contend they should enjoy the same privileges due to their legal occupancy. After several incidents involving equipment damage, some societies have adopted these additional fees.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/maintenance-paid-but-noida-rwas-want-tenants-to-shell-out-extra-fees-for-using-gym-pool/133363801?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-81904/133363801.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Bihar RERA launches drive to speed up dues recovery from defaulting builders", "para": "In a bid to streamline the reclaiming of dues from negligent builders, Bihar Rera has kicked off a specialized campaign. A commendable step saw a defaulting builder settling a complainant with Rs 13 lakh following Rera\u2019s directive. The campaign seeks to facilitate homebuyers in recovering their investments more swiftly, minimizing the need for legal action. In another case, Rs 7 lakh were recovered from a different builder.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/rera/bihar-rera-launches-drive-to-speed-up-dues-recovery-from-defaulting-builders/133363718?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-353476/133363718.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "rera"}]}